# Risk surfaces: how much human and agent review attention a change to a path deserves.
# The pre-push review reads this file from the BASE branch, so a PR cannot lower the tier of its
# own files. Format: `<tier> <glob>`, last match wins. A glob containing `/` is anchored at the
# repository root; one without matches at any depth.
#
# critical  — what a read returns or a write persists: transactions and the transaction log,
#             column-family routing, encodings, commit, backup/restore, file locking, snapshot
#             and bounds handling in iterators, native lifetime and teardown
# sensitive — authentication, authorization, secrets
# hot       — per-call paths where a regression is a performance incident
# ordinary  — overrides a broader line above it

